WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.930
Samsung just announced their latest flagship
tablet, The Tab S6 and I’ve got to say that

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:10.040
this is probably the best tablet for replacing
a laptop, even better than the iPad Pro with

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.600
its impressive iPad OS update scheduled for
full release this fall.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.000
We’ll talk about exactly why the Tab S6
is likely a better choice in just a bit, but

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.600
first, let me tell you why I’m excited for
it.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.170
Just a few months ago Samsung released the
S5e, a budget tablet that I genuinely really

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:31.960
liked but told most people not to buy it in
my full review, but the S6 changes that suggestion.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:37.230
I love how thin and lightweight the S5e is,
the loud quad speakers, and on top of that,

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.000
the gorgeous AM OLED 16:10 display which is
great for media consumption.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.219
With that said, there were a few big downsides
that made it hard to recommend.

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:51.620
The first was the Snapdragon 670 CPU which
is mediocre for today's standard and really

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.870
worrisome if you want to keep it for a few
years.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:59.399
Paired with the midrange CPU is a weak GPU
which made gaming a very poor experience and

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:03.489
lastly, there is no pen support which is a
dealbreaker for some people.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:08.450
We’ll the new S6 fixed all of those things
giving us pen support like the previous Tab

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.890
S4 and a CPU that can handle everything you
throw at it.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:16.100
They’ve made some physical changes like
removing the side-mounted fingerprint scanner

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.979
opting for an optical under-display scanner.

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:24.539
I have to say that this is a very interesting
choice given their flagship phones use ultrasonic

00:01:24.539 --> 00:01:25.539
sensors.

00:01:25.539 --> 00:01:29.560
We also have an updated keyboard and a new
pen that's included in the box and connects

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.810
magnetically on the back.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:37.330
We also now have dual-cameras on the back,
one being a 5MP ultrawide lens.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:42.869
Even with these additions, the tablet is only
20grams heavier than the S5e and only 5.7mm

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:48.060
thick, meaning this will still be a fantastic
device for long handheld use, but this video

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.329
isn't just about the hardware, but about how
the new Tab S6 is a better laptop replacement

00:01:53.329 --> 00:01:54.630
than the iPad Pro.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:59.659
Since Vadim recently did a video on how the
iPad Pro is a viable laptop replacement, I

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:05.159
think it would be best to just let him take
over and explain why.

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:09.060
The most important thing that could make the
Tab S6 a better laptop replacement than the

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.510
iPad Pro is a pretty amazing feature called
Samsung Dex.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:16.310
It’s basically an operating system that’s
instantly accessible from an app.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:21.020
What’s so special about it is that it gives
you full cursor support and you get a desktop

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:25.330
layout that’s very similar to Windows 10,
with a start menu and app shortcuts right

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.330
on the desktop.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:31.490
You get incredible multitasking with rearrangeable
windows and apps minimize into the menu bar

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:32.490
as well.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:36.850
Not only that, but you get traditional drag
and drop file storage support, just like we’re

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.250
used to on a Windows or Mac computer.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:39.250
And for years, Android has been known for
having much better file transfer support,

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.250
compared to Apple who is really only getting
actually usable transfer support with the

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.250
upcoming iPadOS.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.430
To put the cherry on top, the available keyboard
case actually comes with a trackpad!

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.950
Now we won’t be able to tell how well it
works until we get the Tab S6 in our office,

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:52.910
but the built-in trackpad makes it feel so
much more like an actual laptop, especially

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:53.910
while in Dex!

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:59.390
While Apple’s iPad does get mouse support,
it just mimics touch input instead of actually

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:03.830
registering clicks, so you can’t really
use it like you would on a desktop computer.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:08.420
With the Tab S6, though, you can plug it into
an external monitor, connect a bluetooth mouse

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:12.850
and keyboard, and turn on Dex to have a legitimate
desktop computer experience.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:17.960
And to make it even better, the Tab S6 comes
with the stylus in the box, unlike the Apple

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.920
Pencil, which you have to purchase separately
for $130.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:29.180
The best part is that the 256GB of storage
model only costs $729, and it comes with 8GB

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.180
of RAM compared to the iPad Pros 4GB of RAM.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:37.690
And if you buy the keyboard case before September
22, you can get it for half off.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:43.010
That means that with the Tab S6, you can get
a complete setup with 256GB of storage, the

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:49.610
Snapdragon 855 processor, 8GB of RAM, the
stylus and the trackpad-packing keyboard case

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:53.170
for a total of $819.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:58.510
The 11” iPad Pro with 256GB of storage,
the Apple Pencil and the Smart Keyboard Folio

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:06.210
will cost you $1107, so you’re saving almost
$300 by going with the Tab S6 instead.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:10.410
But while the Tab S6 looks incredible on the
spec sheet, things may change when we get

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.670
our hands on it and actually compare the two
side by side.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:17.250
For example, there are way more apps on the
iPad that work really great compared to some

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:22.660
Android apps that suffer from poor optimization
and resolution issues on Samsung’s tablets.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:26.950
So if you want to see us compare the Tab S6
and the iPad Pro, make sure to click the circle

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:27.950
above to subscribe.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:34.620
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next one!

